[gravestone_desc]
inputtype=autoint
outputtype=string
default=
transmit=yes
val=A simple plaque, bearing the name of the deceased.<br><br>(Everyone has this by default.)
val=A dignified little flag flutters in the breeze.
val=A simple little gravestone.
val=An ornately carved gravestone.
val=An elaborate font. As water collects in the bowl, it symbolises new life and hope.
val=A monolithic memorial stone bearing a selection of emblems.
val=The four-pointed star is universally recognised as the symbol of Saradomin.
val=This serpentine sigil represents the ruthless Zamorak.
val=Favoured by humans of a mystical or druidic inclination.
val=Followers of Bandos are now scarce, but this symbol is still used by those who remember that violent god.
val=Armadyl's love of winged creatures is represented by this elegant symbol. Little else is remembered of him.
val=Adventurers often request this symbol, although its origin and meaning have become obscure in the centuries since the god wars.
val=The ultimate marker for a grave, this statue evokes intimations of mortality in all who are faced with it.

